# Fleet votes with callbacks days or weeks later. House style: content/STYLE.md.
# Both sides of every vote are reasonable people being reasonable.

# --- Fleet portrait -----------------------------------------------------------
card dec_photo
type decision
cat mission
days 2 3
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean warm fly decline
text Public affairs wants a fleet portrait: eight ships in one frame, with Earth filling the sky behind them. That means eight ships a hundred metres apart, and the propellant to get there.
option fly | Fly the formation | Eight ships close to a hundred metres for twelve minutes. {A} {A:takes} it from the end of the line: seven ships, Earth, and the edge of {A}'s own hull.
  set photo_taken
  res fuel -2
  morale A 4
option decline | Politely decline | The fleet sends a polite no and a very good photo of a single ship.

# --- Water recovery -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_water
type decision
cat repair
days 14 21
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave degrade strip
when cond A ok
when home A
text Water recovery on {A}'s ship is down to 93 percent from 98. {A} {A:wants} to strip the processor now. {B} {B:wants} to run it degraded and fix it when things are calmer.
option strip | Strip it now | The processor spends nine hours in pieces on the deck. {A} {A:finds} a clogged filter and a check valve installed backwards at the factory. Recovery is back to 98 percent by dinner.
  set water_fixed
  who water_fix_who A
  mark t_water
  res spares -1
  trait A curious 3
option degrade | Run it degraded | {A}'s ship goes on water rationing, and the other seven trim {A:theirs} a notch so there's a bag to send at the next window. {A} {A:logs} the rate hourly; it slips a tenth at a time.
  set water_rationed
  who water_who A
  morale A -3

card water_fail
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 22 22
roles A B
when flag water_rationed
when is A water_who
when apart B A
when cond B ok
when home A
when !is B eva_who
text The degraded water processor on {A}'s ship quits at 04:00 on a crossing day. {A} {A:drinks} from the reserve bag through a morning of {B}'s prebreathe while the next ship closes up. By afternoon {B} {B:is} across with the spare valve; water flows by dinner. It tops out at ninety-five percent, for good.
do move B A
do bond A B 8
do res spares -1
do clr water_rationed

card water_good
type beat
cat repair
due
once
days 23 34
roles A
when flag water_fixed
when is A water_fix_who
when since t_water >= 9
when home A
text The water processor on {A}'s ship passes its thousandth hour since the strip-down, still at 98 percent. {A} {A:opens} the panel just to look at the check valve, facing the right way now, and {A:closes} it: "{Av}"
do morale A 2

# --- Clocks -----------------------------------------------------------------
card dec_clock
type decision
cat mission
days 4 30
weight 6
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious shift keep
text Mission Control proposes moving the fleet's clocks two hours forward, to line up with the ground team's shifts. {A} {A:is} for it. {B} {B:has} seen how this study ended last time.
option shift | Change the clocks | The fleet shifts its clocks. Everyone is tired for three days, then fine. {B} {B:files} the last page in one word: "Predicted."
  set clock_shifted
option keep | Keep fleet time | The fleet keeps its clocks. The ground team adjusts instead, and sends a photo of the night shift's pizza.
  set clock_kept

card clock_shift_back
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 31 34
roles A
when flag clock_shifted
text Since the clock change, the ground's morning is the fleet's morning. {A} {A:asks} a question at nine and {A:has} the answer by lunch, from someone who has also just had coffee. It still feels like cheating.

card clock_keep_back
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 31 34
roles A
when flag clock_kept
text Since the fleet kept its own clock, the ground's handover lands in the fleet's first coffee. {A} {A:knows} them all by name now, and they know {A}'s coffee order, for all the good it does.

# --- Course correction -------------------------------------------------------
card dec_trim
type decision
cat mission
days 15 23
weight 9
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean brave now wait
text Navigation shows the fleet drifting toward the edge of the arrival corridor. {A} {A:wants} a small correction burn now. {B} {B:wants} to wait for the scheduled burn, which costs more but leaves time to check the solution three times.
option now | Burn now | A short, clean burn. {A} {A:watches} the residuals come in under a millimetre per second, and {A:writes} the number on the back of a hand.
  set trim_early
  set trim_done
  res fuel -1
option wait | Wait and check | The solution gets checked three times, then a fourth. The scheduled burn goes off on time and on target, and {B} {B:lets} the computer fly it.
  set trim_late
  set trim_done
  res fuel -3

card trim_callback
type event
cat mission
due
once
days 29 33
roles A
when flag trim_early
when cond A ok
text The latest navigation fix comes in: the fleet sits well inside the arrival corridor, a few tens of kilometres off centre, still riding that small early burn. {A} {A:writes} the number up beside Earth's last decent photo.
do morale A 3

card trim_callback_late
type event
cat mission
due
once
days 29 33
roles A
when flag trim_late
when cond A ok
text The latest navigation fix comes in: dead centre of the arrival corridor. The checked burn cost more than the quick one would have, and {A} {A:reruns} the propellant table. It still says yes. {A} {A:stops} running it. "{Av}"
do morale A 2

# --- Arrival: dust storm over the landing region -------------------------------
card dust_report
type event
cat mission
days 28 35
weight 1
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} {A:pulls} the morning weather from the Mars orbiters: a dust storm, building over the landing zone. On the map it's a brown thumbprint. {A} {A:lays} a ruler across it, then {A:lays} the ruler across the backup site.
do set dust_seen
do mark t_dust

card dust_worse
type event
cat mission
due
once
days 32 38
roles A
when flag dust_seen
when since t_dust >= 3
when !fired dec_arrival
when cond A ok
when since t_flash >= 4
text The dust storm over the landing zone has doubled overnight; the brown thumbprint covers it with room to spare. On the shared map, the ruler line no longer reaches clear ground.
do open dec_arrival

card dec_arrival
type decision
cat arrival
days 33 38
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
when flag dust_seen
lean warm wait hold
text The storm over the landing zone is still growing; the flight director wants the crew's call. {A} {A:wants} to hold the arrival plan and trust the margins. {B} {B:wants} to skim the atmosphere into a long parking orbit and wait it out, at a real cost in food.
option hold | Hold the plan | The arrival plan stands. {A} {A:posts} the entry numbers for the worst-case dust load where everyone can see.
  set arrive_hold
option wait | Long orbit, wait | Aerocapture, then the long orbit. {B} {B:recomputes} every margin. Thin, and enough.
  set arrive_wait
  who wait_who B
  res fuel -4

